✈️ Entity Relationship Diagram (ERD) — JetBlue Flight Booking System

The Entity Relationship Diagram (ERD) illustrates how data is organized and how different entities in the JetBlue Flight Booking System relate to one another.
It provides a visual overview of the three core tables — flights, passengers, and bookings — along with their attributes and relationships.

![ERD Diagram](docs/)


🔗 Relationships Summary

One flight can have many bookings.

One passenger can make many bookings.

Therefore, the relationship between flights and passengers is many-to-many, represented through the bookings table.

🧩 ERD Visualization

The diagram below (saved as docs/ERD.png) visually represents these relationships:

Primary keys (PK) are shown with a key icon.

Foreign keys (FK) link related tables.

Dashed lines represent relationships between entities.

📁 File path: docs/ERD.png

💬 In summary

This ERD ensures:

Data integrity via primary and foreign keys.

Efficient querying through normalization.

Scalability, allowing easy addition of new entities such as aircrafts, crew, or payments in the future.
